
cff-version: 1.2.0

message: >-
  If you use these MATLAB codes in your research,
  please cite this software release and the associated
  research article when available.

title: >-
  Analytical MATLAB Codes for Fine Structure,
  Rotational Hyperfine Splitting, and Superradiant
  Widths in Myers-Perry-AdS

authors:
  - given-names: "Hamed"
    family-names: "Ramezani"

type: software

version: "1.0.2"
date-released: "2026-10-30"

doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23815105"

repository-code: "https://github.com/H-rmzi/MP-AdS_GA"

abstract: >-
  MATLAB codes supporting the analytical investigation
  of massive scalar quasibound states around small,
  singly spinning Myers-Perry-AdS black holes.
  Three scripts reproduce effective-potential diagrams,
  gravitational fine structure, rotational hyperfine
  splitting, and horizon-induced damping and
  superradiant growth rates.

  An additional self-contained MATLAB program reproduces
  the static resonant coefficient Q_out and the logarithmic
  and finite coefficients A_N and B_N of the mixed
  rotational-resonant spectral corrections for D=7,
  l=2, and radial overtones N=0,1. It also implements
  an independent node-free radial consistency check.

  The analytical supplement was successfully executed
  using MATLAB R2025b. The codes evaluate analytical
  approximations and do not implement an independent
  numerical solver for the full rotating quasibound-state
  eigenvalue problem.

keywords:
  - Myers-Perry-AdS
  - Gravitational atom
  - Massive scalar field
  - Fine structure
  - Rotational hyperfine splitting
  - Superradiance
  - Resonant response
  - Matched asymptotic expansions
  - MATLAB

